# Purged-history markers, read by history-gate (same directory). One commit per
# line: <full sha> <repo> <what it is>. Each is the OLDEST commit of a history
# that a secret purge removed — its root, or the first commit after the prefix
# the rewrite left byte-identical — so every removed commit has one of these in
# its ancestry. Derive a new one as: the commits of `git rev-list --parents
# <old tip> --not <new main>` none of whose parents are in that same list.
# Adding a purge = appending its markers here; nothing else changes.
